---
// 3.5 — Pin versions and document: lock file snippet
// Uses obviously generic tool names to avoid implying real version compatibility claims
---

<div class="pin-wrap">
  <div class="pin-label">VALIDATION.md — VERSION PINNING</div>
  <div class="pin-file">
    <div class="pf-header">
      <div class="pf-filename">versions.lock</div>
    </div>
    <div class="pf-body">
      <div class="pf-comment"># Tools emulated and validated against</div>
      <div class="pf-blank"></div>
      <div class="pf-section">[tools]</div>
      <div class="pf-entry">
        <span class="pf-key">tool-a</span>
        <span class="pf-eq"> = </span>
        <span class="pf-val">"1.0.0"</span>
        <span class="pf-comment-inline">  # validated: 2024-11-03</span>
      </div>
      <div class="pf-entry">
        <span class="pf-key">tool-b</span>
        <span class="pf-eq"> = </span>
        <span class="pf-val">"2.3.1"</span>
        <span class="pf-comment-inline">  # validated: 2024-11-07</span>
      </div>
      <div class="pf-entry">
        <span class="pf-key">tool-c</span>
        <span class="pf-eq"> = </span>
        <span class="pf-val">"0.9.4"</span>
        <span class="pf-comment-inline">  # validated: 2024-11-09</span>
      </div>
      <div class="pf-blank"></div>
      <div class="pf-section">[validation]</div>
      <div class="pf-entry">
        <span class="pf-key">methodology</span>
        <span class="pf-eq"> = </span>
        <span class="pf-val">"VALIDATION.md"</span>
      </div>
      <div class="pf-entry">
        <span class="pf-key">test_data</span>
        <span class="pf-eq"> = </span>
        <span class="pf-val">"benchmarks/data/README.md"</span>
      </div>
      <div class="pf-entry">
        <span class="pf-key">reference_outputs</span>
        <span class="pf-eq"> = </span>
        <span class="pf-val">"benchmarks/expected/"</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="pin-note">
    Future maintainers — and your future self — need to know exactly what was validated against what. Ambiguity erodes trust.
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .pin-wrap {
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .pin-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .pin-file {
    background: #0d0d0d;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
    border-radius: 6px;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }

  .pf-header {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.07);
    padding: 6px var(--space-md);
  }

  .pf-filename {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
  }

  .pf-body {
    padding: var(--space-md);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .pf-comment {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.25);
  }

  .pf-blank {
    height: 6px;
  }

  .pf-section {
    color: var(--rust-400);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  .pf-entry {
    padding-left: var(--space-md);
  }

  .pf-key   { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .pf-eq    { color: var(--text-tertiary); }
  .pf-val   { color: rgba(74, 222, 128, 0.85); }

  .pf-comment-inline {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);
  }

  .pin-note {
    font-size: 0.83rem;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
    padding-top: var(--space-sm);
    line-height: 1.6;
    font-style: italic;
  }
</style>
